# decTest integer-power vectors
#
# Extracted mechanically (scripts noted in SPEC.md) from the IBM / Mike
# Cowlishaw "General Decimal Arithmetic Testcases" v2.62, file power.decTest,
# "Reproduced with permission ... Copyright 1997, 2009 by International
# Business Machines Corporation" -- https://speleotrove.com/decimal/dectest.html
# See NOTICE.
#
# Format: id|base|exponent|expected|expected_exponent
# Test IDs are the source file's, kept for traceability.
#
# Cases NOT wired, and why:
#   543    context-precision flag (Inexact/Rounded)
#   112    hard flag, no result in this module (overflow)
#   86     special value (NaN/Inf) or non-numeric operand
#   74     hard flag, no result in this module (clamped,subnormal,underflow)
#   55     hard flag, no result in this module (invalid_operation)
#   49     negative exponent (java.math.BigDecimal.pow(int) rejects these too)
#   37     hard flag, no result in this module (subnormal,underflow)
#   31     hard flag, no result in this module (subnormal)
#   23     exponent past the max_result_digits budget
#   20     non-integer exponent (GDA general power; needs exp/ln - out of scope)
#   17     out of stated bounds (|exp|>10000 or >1000 coeff digits)
#   16     zero result (module prints bare "0", cannot show GDA signed/scaled zero)

